FINDING 2 - preset sync REPAIRED:
$ systemctl --user reset-failed ao-lmstudio-preset-sync.service /.path
$ systemctl --user start ao-lmstudio-preset-sync.path   -> active
$ /ALWAYSON/scripts/sync-lmstudio-readme-preset.sh
  WROTE .../ALWAYSON - FULL CONTEXT.preset.json (891324 bytes, sha d43b05aaff1c7656)
  state hash now == README hash (was stale 7566377a from Oct-2); JSON parses.
Root cause: >=5 rapid README writes on Oct 2 tripped systemd's start limit; both
units stuck failed, path unit stopped watching (README changed Oct 4 -> preset
never regenerated). Fix: reset-failed + StartLimitIntervalSec=300 and
StartLimitBurst=60 added to [Unit], daemon-reload, manual trigger ->
"Finished ..." (inactive = oneshot OK), path still active.
Work-product consumers (answer to operator Q): repo-wide grep finds ONLY the
generator script; no automation in OpenClaw/Cline/dashboard reads the preset.
Its consumer is the operator manually - the preset appears in the LM Studio
desktop GUI preset list for GUI chats.

FINDING 3 - lms-key-2 KEPT, chmod 600 (documented policy exception):
Reversible probe: file moved aside -> `lms ps` rc=1 with
  "ENOENT: no such file or directory, open '.../.internal/lms-key-2'"
-> file restored (sha unchanged), `lms ps` OK. lms CLI source shows
  auth = { clientIdentifier:"lms-cli", clientPasskey: lmsKey + lmsKey2 }
with lmsKey2 read from this path, and an UNGUARDED readFile in the connect
path - deleting it breaks `lms`, which breaks ao-lmstudio.service (supervisor
uses lms load/ps). It is the CLI<->daemon IPC passkey half, NOT the HTTP API
token (that lives in KDE Wallet entry lmstudio-api-key). Vendor-hardcoded path:
it cannot be relocated to the wallet. $ chmod 600 -> verified mode 600.

